---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const steps = [
  {
    title: 'Install the connector, once',
    text: 'One command on your workstation or on your cluster’s login node, then sign in with your MDXplora account.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Your machine appears in MDXplora',
    text: 'It shows up under “Run on”, beside MDXplora’s own GPUs, with what it has: its GPUs and, on a cluster, its scheduler.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Choose where each study runs',
    text: 'Build the study in the browser, pick the machine and press Run. Each choice shows the estimated time before you commit.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The connector does the work',
    text: 'It picks the job up, runs the study there or submits it to SLURM, and sends progress back to your browser.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Compute"
  description="Run MDXplora studies on GPUs we provide, or on your own workstation or cluster, chosen per study."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Compute</span>
      <h1>Our GPUs, or yours.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        No GPU to own and nothing to install. When you do have machines, connect them and choose for each study where it
        runs.
      </p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="/contact/?topic=early-access">
          Join early access
        </a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="/#how">
          How a study runs
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container grid-3">
      <h2 class="visually-hidden">Why run studies on MDXplora</h2>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Nothing to install</h3>
        <p>Open a browser and sign in. No environment to build and no drivers to match to a CUDA version.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>The same study anywhere</h3>
        <p>
          A study is one Config. It runs the same on our GPUs and on yours, and it can be downloaded whole, with its
          data and its record, whenever you want it.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Chosen per study</h3>
        <p>Our GPUs when you have none, your own workstation or cluster when you do.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Your own compute</span>
        <h2>Our interface, your machines.</h2>
        <p>
          Your machine asks MDXplora for work, the way a mail app checks for new mail. Nothing reaches into your
          network, so there are no ports to open and nothing for IT to configure.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps">
        {steps.map((s, i) => (
          <li class="card">
            <span class="step-number">{i + 1}</span>
            <h3>{s.title}</h3>
            <p>{s.text}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <div class="notes grid-2">
        <div>
          <h3>Your data can stay where it is</h3>
          <p>Trajectories can remain on your own storage, with only the study records and reports shown in MDXplora.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>It only runs MD studies</h3>
          <p>
            The connector runs validated Configs and nothing else. It never executes code sent to it, which is what
            makes it straightforward for an IT department to approve.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container closing">
      <h2>Tell us what you would run.</h2>
      <p>
        Early access is opening to a small number of groups first. Tell us about your systems and your compute, and we
        will be in touch.
      </p>
      <a class="button button-primary" href="/contact/?topic=early-access">
        Join early access
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .cta {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }
  .steps {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }
  .step-number {
    display: inline-grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--badge-gradient);
    color: #fff;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .notes {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }
  .notes h3 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }
  .notes p {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }
  .closing {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 40rem;
  }
  .closing h2 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
  }
  .closing p {
    margin: 1rem auto 2rem;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .steps {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .steps {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
